Have been playing a Priest recently (after ascending a Valk).
Exactly how do the starting Priest foods work?  I assume that
garlic is good against vampires and wolfbane is against
wolves.  Does one eat them to obtain intrinsic combat advantage
or do you wield them against the opponent?  Does wolfbane work
on all little d's?

On a related note, I like the Priest's ability to detect
curse/blessed status, saves the time waiting for the pet to
walk on item.  This would be a highly desireable intrinsic to
have.  Perhaps other characters could gain it by eating temple
priests or make it part of becoming the HoE/EoB/CoS that most
people hate.  To maintain balance since the Priest would not get
something for it, how about letting the Priest have
professional courtesy at any temple, he can pray to his god
regardless of the alignment.  For altars, he would still need
to convert, however.

